<title>SENEGAL: Senegal offers stake in state airline.</title>
<headline>Senegal offers stake in state airline.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal said on Monday it was seeking a strategic partner for its national carrier Air Senegal as part of its privatisation programme.</p>
<p>&quot;The government of Senegal pledges to cede 51 percent of the capital of the company to a strategic partner,&quot; the state privatisation committee said in a statement.</p>
<p>Air Senegal has a Twin otter plane of 18 seats, and 116 staff, an official of Air Senegal told Reuters.</p>
<p>The closing date for tenders is July 14.</p>
</text>
